 ./pass.py ls
 ```
 
+## Sync
+
+Not in the original `pass`: `pass.py sync` trades the store with other devices (a phone) through a
+*drop zone*, a directory every device can reach and nobody has to trust: a local path (a USB stick,
+a synced folder) or `sftp://user@host[:port][/dir]`.
+
+Each device publishes one file there, `<device>.bundle.gpg`: a git bundle of its whole history,
+signed with its OpenPGP key and encrypted to every device. The drop zone sees those files and
+nothing else: no entry name, no history. This computer is the owner of the store: it takes another
+device's commits only as a fast-forward, only when each is signed by that device, and only when
+they change nothing but entries (never a `.gpg-id`, never an extension).
+
+```bash
+# Once: name this computer, say where the drop zone is and which key signs
+./pass.py sync setup pc sftp://drop@example.org:2222 <own-key-fingerprint>
+./pass.py sync peer phone <phone-key-fingerprint>     # its public key must be in gpg
+
+./pass.py sync push            # publish the store
+./pass.py sync fetch           # take what the other devices published
+./pass.py sync log phone       # their commits, and who signed each
+./pass.py sync diff phone      # the same, decrypted
+./pass.py sync merge phone     # take them, then publish
+./pass.py sync                 # where everything stands
+```
+
+`ssh` options (a key, a port in `~/.ssh/config`) apply as usual; more can be set with
+`git config pass-sync.sftp-options "-i ~/.ssh/dropzone"` in the store. The store must be a git
+repository (`pass git init`). The protocol, a drop zone server and a phone client live in
+[c4ffein-work/playground](https://github.com/c4ffein-work/playground), under `ios-apps/apps/pass`.
+
 ## Testing
 
 The Python implementation is designed to be fully compatible with the original bash script and should pass all the tests in `submodules/password-store/tests/`. Additional tests have also been written in an automated way, see [the documentation about Claude Code](chat_history/00-INDEX.md)
